Application binaries
--------------------
third_party/go-licenses.csv lists license families and retained license paths
for packages linked by argus, argus-manager and argus-hostd.
third_party/go-modules.txt records their module versions. Original license
and NOTICE files are in third_party/licenses/go. Go runtime/standard-library
notices are in third_party/licenses/go-runtime.

Web assets
----------
third_party/components.tsv records bundled assets and infrastructure projects.
third_party/license-sources.tsv records the retained project license URLs.
third_party/web-assets.sha256 identifies the exact vendored files, including
snapshots whose upstream release version is not recorded. Original notices
remain in web/static/vendor and are copied into third_party/licenses/web.
noVNC's preferred JavaScript source is distributed in web/static/vendor/novnc.
Its pako fork is based on 1.0.3; retained DES notices cover additional
upstream contributions.

Images and operating system
---------------------------
Application images and the host helper export carry this notice and
third_party under /usr/share/doc/argus. Argus OS and derived ISOs carry the
same files, installed-package versions in third_party/os-packages.tsv and
package copyright files in third_party/licenses/os. Distribution license
texts remain in /usr/share/common-licenses and /usr/share/doc.
Infrastructure source references and Go dependency notices are retained in
third_party/infrastructure. This inventory covers upstream command packages,
including commands beyond those shipped by Argus. Embedded K3s utilities
have their own third_party/k3s-root-manifest.csv and licenses/k3s-root notices.
Their matching Buildroot source archive includes upstream configurations,
patches, license manifests and package sources.

Runtime-downloaded images/charts are identified in components.tsv; their
upstream distributions have their own notices and source obligations.
Bundled KubeVirt/CDI operator manifests have resource and Go memory settings
adjusted in os/Dockerfile; upstream license terms continue to apply.
Build-only tools are not included in the Argus runtime.

Source distribution
-------------------
Argus source and build scripts: https://github.com/sindef/argus
Use the source revision associated with the released image, not a moving branch.
Go module names and exact versions identify their upstream sources.
OS package source names and exact versions are recorded in os-packages.tsv.
Release source archives accompany images at https://github.com/sindef/argus/releases.
Archives over the hosting limit are split into .part-* files; concatenate
parts in filename order before extracting. SHA256SUMS records collected files.
Distributors must provide matching source or another license-permitted source
arrangement for covered copyleft components.
